# 9. DEPENDENCY DIRECTION (THE GOLDEN RULE)

Subsystems must obey:

```
Low-level → High-level, never the reverse
```

Examples:

Smart Ingestor may depend on EntityFactory →  
But EntityFactory may not depend on Smart Ingestor.

Decoherence may depend on Neo4j →  
But Neo4j adapter may not depend on Decoherence.

AIRPG may depend on Query Engine →  
But Query Engine may not depend on AIRPG.

This rule guarantees architectural longevity.

