13. GLOSSARY
Core Concepts
Canon
Truth established by human authority following the Gospel Principle. Canon-locked data overrides all contradictions and cannot be changed by AI inference.
Decoherence
The process by which an entity transitions from superposition (unresolved state) to eigenstate (collapsed, canonical state) when observed by players or simulation.
Eigenstate
A collapsed, definitive entity state after observation. Stored as versioned snapshots with full provenance.
OCEAN Model
Big Five personality framework used for NPC psychological modeling:
Openness: Creativity, curiosity (0-1)
Conscientiousness: Discipline, reliability (0-1)
Extraversion: Sociability, assertiveness (0-1)
Agreeableness: Compassion, cooperation (0-1)
Neuroticism: Emotional instability, anxiety (0-1)
Superposition
An unresolved entity state before observation. Entity exists with minimal metadata until player interaction triggers collapse.
Architecture Terms
Subsystem
A bounded module under src/<subsystem>/ with its own orchestrator, contract document, governance rules, and defined import boundaries. Examples: Smart Ingestor, Decoherence Engine, Query Engine.
Orchestrator
The single entry point for a subsystem. Coordinates module execution, manages context flow, and enforces pipeline order. Only orchestrators may call LLMs.
Module Contract
Defines a module's purpose, public API, inputs, outputs, dependencies, and constraints. Ensures AI-safe implementation and prevents architectural drift.
Subsystem Contract
Top-level governance document for a subsystem defining architecture, pass order, integration points, allowed/forbidden imports, and testing requirements.
Handoff Dossier
Comprehensive state document generated after each implementation session. Contains completed modules, pending work, public APIs, integration rules, and hard constraints.
Governance Terms
Gospel Principle
Humans have final authority on all canonical lore decisions. AI provides suggestions but cannot override human judgment on truth.
Universal Implementation Template
Standardized prompt structure for building subsystems. Enforces repo scanning, module-by-module development, diff-only editing, and handoff dossier generation.
Dependency Direction Rule (Golden Rule)
Low-level modules may depend on high-level modules, never the reverse. Prevents circular dependencies and ensures architectural scalability.
Data Terms
Entity
A graph node representing a character, location, faction, item, or event. Contains properties, relationships, and metadata.
Relationship
A directed edge connecting entities. Examples: LEADS, ALLIED_WITH, CAUSED, AT_LOCATION.
Canon Status
Classification of data confidence:
LOCKED: Immutable, overrides contradictions
TBD: Placeholder for future human decision
PLACEHOLDER: Temporary, marked for replacement
INFERRED: AI-generated from context
State Vector
Complete representation of an entity's properties at a point in time. Used by Decoherence Engine for temporal resolution.
Confidence Score
0-1 value indicating certainty of inferred properties. Scores below threshold trigger human review.
Simulation Terms
Evolution Operator
Entity-type-specific logic determining how entities change over elapsed time when unobserved. Examples: NPC_EvolutionOperator, Faction_EvolutionOperator.
Observation Context
Minimal, deterministic context used during entity collapse. Contains connected entities, environmental state, observer ID, time delta, and collapse seed.
Observer Cache
Session-level memory tracking which entities are already collapsed. Prevents redundant resolution and enforces session consistency.
Collapse Seed
Deterministic value ensuring same inputs always produce same eigenstate. Critical for reproducibility and debugging.
